00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.216
incredibly stuffy

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.884
, especially for

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.786
men working in factories under tin sheds.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.553
Have you noticed

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.788
how hot and stuffy it is?

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.890
According to meteorological research from Academia Sinica,

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.525
summers used to last 90 days,

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.128
but now they've increased to 120 or even 140 days.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:28.828
It's getting hotter and hotter

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.030
, and what's particularly noticeable is that

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.132
you might not remember summers

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.999
being this hot

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:33.800
when you were a child. No

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.968
? According to statistics,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.803
we now have to contend with summer

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:37.971
for

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.205
more than half the year

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.507
, especially in Taiwan,

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.208
where factories, dilapidated

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.310
tin-roofed buildings,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.478
snack

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.546
stalls, Vietnamese restaurants, and even

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.448
car roofs are everywhere.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:48.982
So in this episode,

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:49.916
we're going to talk about

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.052
how to use simple construction methods

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.353
to make your home

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.254
a bit cooler.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:54.687
For example,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.722
right across from

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.556
me in Dali

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.425
is my old high school.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.692
In Dali,

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.662
you'll definitely see many small and medium-sized factories

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.065
or small processing spaces.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.299
We often tell people that learning

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.067
engineering from elementary school

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:07.934
can lead to big profits.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.735
One part of

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.602
that is patents.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.371
If you can... Using a single mindset

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.305
, an idea

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.840
, and understanding the effects of science

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.674
can help you

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.642
make your entire building,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.077
whether it's your home or a factory

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.178
,

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:18.878
much more breathable

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.712
and cool

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.814
, and also change the lighting.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.381
For example,

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.916
I'm currently in a factory,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.651
and it looks like a factory

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.618
, but doesn't it seem

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.619
particularly bright?

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.388
Photographer, please shift to the left or right. Do I have any lighting?

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.089
(No)

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.590
Because usually when we shoot, we use supplemental lighting,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.124
especially when we

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.692
've shot traditional factories

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.760
or

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.095
factory machinery.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:35.728
We always use lighting.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.463
But this

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.130
doesn't need lighting

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.264
, and it's very cool.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.566
Now, if you look back and

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.234
look at the history of this ironworks,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.069
it should look much better than what I'm seeing now. It's

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.804
even older than my dad,

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.473
so why does it look bright

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:47.440
and cool?

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.342
You know, there's a big principle

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.110
and a key point

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.778
, which is the engineering principle we're going to talk about today.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.846
Opening

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:53.613
a skylight in a factory

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.914
sounds unlucky,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:55.982
but actually, in a house

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.583
, a building

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.884
, or even a metal factory,

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.719
you don't need to make any major changes.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.387
If you understand the engineering principles

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.123
and the principles of thermal dynamics

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.457
, simply opening a skylight will make

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.458
the entire environment

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.926
very cool.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.727
The reason for

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.561
this episode

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.229
is that

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.130
many people might wonder why

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.097
so few people are willing to work

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.098
in metal factories

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.433
or traditional industries—

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.534
because the environment is terrible,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.269
dark, and... It's hot,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.137
that's normal.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:17.971
A tin roof

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.272
can reach 70 degrees Celsius

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.773
under direct sunlight

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.575
—enough to cook an egg if you crack it on, and

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.711
blisters if you put your hand on it for two seconds.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.180
That's the heat of a factory roof.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.747
That's why

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.315
we have many building materials in the industry

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.683
, including heat-insulating materials

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.352
, fireproof materials

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.953
, and materials that can block heat. We used to put

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:34.587
polystyrene foam or

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.655
asbestos next to it , and

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.856
many other heat-insulating materials

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:37.957
. Are these useful? Yes, they

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.994
are.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.297
But what people might not understand is

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.331
the chimney effect , which

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.099
I want to talk about today

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.967
. And the engineering modification I'm going to talk about today

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.335
isn't just for tin factories

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.703
or ordinary factories;

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.705
it can be used even in… Generally,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.606
you can renovate a typical detached house,

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.942
especially a multi-story house, where the effects are particularly noticeable.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.110
Why?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.511
When we used to buy houses,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.112
everyone would say it

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.213
should face south

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.181
or north.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.215
But actually, when the sun rises,

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.082
the house faces east or

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.584
west. So, if your house

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.919
faces east or west,

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.253
especially

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.087
after sunset when the sun is shining from

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.756
the west , the whole house will feel like an oven

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:10.723
– very hot.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.558
Of course, the house's orientation

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.692
is related

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.826
to its temperature .

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.195
Because of Taiwan's climate,

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.863
regardless of the wind direction

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.865
, north-south facing houses tend

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.465
to be

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.700
warmer in winter

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.735
and cooler in summer. But even if

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.970
your house faces south, if

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.072
there's nothing to block the sun from the west... If

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.141
your house is also very hot, it will be very hot.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.976
Traditional

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.411
Taiwanese buildings,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.445
because of their cement and roofs

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.813
, absorb heat during the day

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.248
and need several hours

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.083
to reach a balance with the room temperature

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.751
through natural heat dissipation.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.986
According to data ,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.688
the temperature on the top floor of a detached house at night

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:42.989
is more than 10 degrees Celsius higher

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.224
than the floors below.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.491
So if you live in a detached house

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.694
and climb to a higher floor,

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:49.295
you will feel particularly stuffy

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.663
because heat rises.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.131
However, there is another argument

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.967
: some people

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.501
say that it is cooler to live on higher floors.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.302
Why?

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:56.803
Because firstly,

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.671
it is not affected by the ground temperature, and secondly

00:03:58.671 --> 00:03:59.405
... Another point is that

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.174
the ventilation is relatively good

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.509
, so ventilation is actually very important.

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.510
But why does your house

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.045
keep getting hot and can't dissipate?

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.413
Before we start the experiment,

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.514
we first need to let everyone understand

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.749
what the chimney effect

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.684
is . You should have heard

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.886
of chimneys when you were a child. Santa Claus goes in through a chimney

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.521
, or today when

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:16.956
you are camping and burning a fire

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.224
, in order to prevent the smoke

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.859
from filling your entire tent,

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.460
some people

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.995
will connect a chimney to the

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:22.895
fire. That's a chimney.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.197
If we're going to remove some

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.331
very complex formulas

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.866
or fluid dynamics,

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:27.634
you can think of it this way:

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.902
cold air and hot air are two

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.237
different densities.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:31.738
Hot air has

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.406
more vigorous molecular motion.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.474
When cold air is

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.075
heated,

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.844
its density decreases

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.745
, meaning it becomes lighter.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.846
Conversely,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.047
when the temperature drops,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.315
its density increases,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.750
making it heavier

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.951
and causing it to sink.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.586
This is similar to the chimney effect:

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.154
when heated air

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.156
exchanges with cold air, the hot air rises.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:51.190
If

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.892
this

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.793
is a closed, unventilated space

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.927
,

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:55.528
all the heat will

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.963
accumulate, making

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.331
your home feel

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.065
increasingly hot,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.199
like a sauna

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.134
. Your home

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.969
becomes humid and hot

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.737
, and running

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:05.705
the air conditioner is

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.340
expensive

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.341
and stressful. Plus,

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.809
even when the chimney

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.244
is off, the heat doesn't escape.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.245
But what if

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.446
we utilize this heat

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.714
to

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:15.515
help with

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.383
indoor air convection ? Buying air conditioning is certainly a good option

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.651
, but to save money,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.119
especially in Taiwan where there's a power shortage,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.220
what can

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.288
you do if you don't want to buy

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.956
air conditioning

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.891
or a fan

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:25.658
and don't want to spend electricity?

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.392
Make

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.760
a hole in your ceiling.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.095
When the indoor air

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.330
is heated and convection occurs,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.230
what happens? Imagine

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.665
putting a grinder in your house

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.133
and making a hole in your ceiling.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.802
Finally, the house isn't hot anymore!

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:36.969
Can you feel

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.237
all the heat being blown out? So,

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.906
this is the chimney effect.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.308
Why is the chimney effect so important?

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.376
There are actually three sources

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.544
of heat in your house .

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:45.812
The first is conduction heat,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.380
like the sun shining on a tin

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.448
roof.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.515
When the surface temperature

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.850
reaches 70 degrees Celsius,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.884
this heat travels from the metal

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.453
all the way into the room,

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.088
turning it into an oven or fireplace,

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:55.888
heating

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.156
you up like food inside.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:57.657
The second

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:58.524
is radiant heat

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.592
. During the day, the

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.193
sun

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.828
absorbs the heat from the cement and bricks

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:02.795
, heating them up.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.597
This heated cement and bricks

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.698
act like a hand warmer.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.433
When you return home in the evening

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.768
, it slowly releases the heat

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.103
back into the house.

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:11.270
The outside is cool,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.373
but your house is still hot.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.140
The third type of heat

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.274
is poor convection .

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.943
Because hot air is lighter than cold air,

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.244
it tends to rise.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.345
So, if

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.246
your roof

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.814
doesn't have an outlet, the heat

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:22.348
will accumulate

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.783
at the bottom of the ceiling,

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:24.650
making your house

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.585
like a steamer,

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:26.552
slowly cooking you up.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.854
That's why we see many early

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:28.788
Eastern houses

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:29.655
with pointed roofs

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:30.957
, or modern Japanese houses

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:31.924
with sloping sides

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:32.558
. If you can't

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:33.826
allow air convection,

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:34.360
the hot air

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.928
can't be transferred.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:36.529
This problem

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:37.964
has plagued humanity for a very long time. What

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:39.732
solutions were there in the past?

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:40.333
The first was

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:41.234
exhaust fans

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.001
. The principle

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.702
is fine

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:43.936
—they use airflow to

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.438
expel hot air.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.072
However,

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:46.873
they only ventilate, they

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:47.907
don't allow light in

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.875
. If the bearings break,

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:49.609
they're incredibly

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:50.243
noisy at night , and

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.077
over time, water will seep through

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:51.644
the joints

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:52.912
. Many people have experienced

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:53.946
this; after a few years,

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.715
leaks become a problem.

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:56.215
The second,

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.016
more advanced

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.518
option, is electric exhaust fans.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.153
They're even better than exhaust fans

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.354
, but they require electricity and wiring,

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.488
so many people avoid them.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:03.256
If the motor

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:03.790
breaks ,

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.191
you have to climb onto the roof for repairs.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:06.092
In the summer sun,

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:06.959
you'll still

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:07.994
get sunburned

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:08.728
climbing up

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:09.996
, and

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:11.464
your electricity meter will keep running,

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:12.765
increasing your

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:13.332
bill .

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.967
The third, which many factories use,

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.102
is a PC skylight.

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.103
While it allows light in

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:17.904
, it doesn't ventilate.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:18.371
Also,

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:19.672
PC boards age very quickly;

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:20.840
after a few years, they yellow,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.474
visibility

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.275
worsens,

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:22.875
and light transmission

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:23.676
drops by half.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:24.477
More importantly,

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:25.678
when sunlight enters

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:26.813
, heat also enters

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.014
, making the room

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:28.815
even hotter. Therefore,

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:29.816
the factory environment has

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:30.750
deteriorated significantly

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.385
over the past decade. The environment of detached

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.386
houses in Taiwan is like this: tin-roofed houses

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.887
, detached houses with added tin roofs

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.422
, and many factories with tin roofs.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.391
People who want to change but can't change their situation

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.526
take turns switching

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:41.260
between these three imperfect options.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.095
Every summer, they continue to sweat,

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:43.663
leak,

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:44.831
and pay electricity bills.

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:45.665
So,

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:47.333
in increasingly hot Taiwan

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.701
and Asia,

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.569
everyone is thinking,

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:50.870
"Is it possible

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:51.771
to build a chimney

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:53.005
in my house

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:55.541
that preserves the original building structure

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:56.776
, allows for natural light

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:58.110
, doesn't leak ,

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.612
doesn't break during typhoons

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.847
, maintains ventilation

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:01.747
, and basically

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:02.882
requires no maintenance

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:03.816
unless

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:04.717
someone's solar panels are hit

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.752
during a typhoon? "

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.287
The key point is that

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:08.855
it does

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.089
n't need to be plugged in,

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:10.923
doesn't consume electricity

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:11.691
,

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:13.993
lowers the temperature inside the entire house

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.596
, and provides free sunlight.

00:08:16.596 --> 00:08:18.498
This design is like this.

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:20.166
Do you see the aluminum extrusions

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:22.268
inside the weather-resistant powder coating?

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.402
The cross-section

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:24.871
looks roughly like this.

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.072
Don't underestimate this

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.874
thing; it has obtained many patents

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:29.008
and won many awards, including

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:30.643
the London Design Gold Award and

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:32.578
the New York Product Design Silver Award

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.213
. And do you know MUSE?

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.414
MUSE

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.517
nightclub?

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.418
(Permanently closed)

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:42.088
MUSE is a very prestigious and influential

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:43.389
design award in the United States.

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:44.690
It's not just about being shortlisted;

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.691
it's also about winning

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:46.959
a silver medal. There are also

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:48.561
many low-carbon construction methods from all over the world.

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:49.428
That's why we say you should learn

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:51.531
engineering from a young age and grow up to make a lot of money

00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:52.098
with patents.

00:08:52.098 --> 00:08:52.965
And do you know

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:53.966
who holds this patent?

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:54.967
 

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.302
It 's Taiwanese. Just looking at this design

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.571
makes you feel comfortable

00:08:58.571 --> 00:08:59.906
and cool all over

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.340
because there's air conditioning behind you,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:01.774
right? That's right,

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:02.909
because there's air conditioning blowing from behind

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:04.110
. So, most people think, "

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:04.644
If I

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:05.811
wanted to build a chimney

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.213
in my house, I'd just make a hole in the roof

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:07.914
, like

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:09.048
this is my ceiling.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.016
I'd make a hole

00:09:10.016 --> 00:09:10.750
in the ceiling

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:11.484
and open it

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:12.318
up. Then

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:13.119
all the hot air

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:13.853
would rush upwards.

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:14.787
" This is what ordinary

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:15.721
people

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.023
can think of.

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:18.491
Of course, this can't be patented.

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:19.559
Why?

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:20.626
Because it would leak when it rains,

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:21.561
birds would fly in,

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:23.195
and bird droppings would shoot in from the sloping side.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:23.829
Of course, that won't work.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.464
Inside this building

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.332
, you can see

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.767
there's a vent next to it,

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.368
and this vent has

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:30.503
this whooshing...

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:31.504
this circulation

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:32.238
, allowing your hot air

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.439
to flow downwards

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:33.906
. Why?

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:34.507
Because hot air

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.908
is pushed upwards.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:36.709
We usually imagine

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:37.243
 

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.377
it like a chimney

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:39.545
, so we call it the chimney effect

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:41.080
. It's actually a principle of thermal buoyancy.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.081
Do you remember

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:43.149
Mr. Abu Dhabi,

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:44.250
that very rich

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.217
man

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:45.985
? When we

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:47.954
filmed a video in Abu Dhabi,

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:49.822
I bought a set of Abu Dhabi clothes

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.324
for the whole company. Do you know why

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:52.058
I'm the coolest

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:52.925
? Think of it like

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:53.626
the chimney effect

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:55.194
in a desert climate like Abu Dhabi

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:56.495
. We've actually been to the desert

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:57.563
; the heat rises,

00:09:57.563 --> 00:09:58.497
and that heat drives

00:09:58.497 --> 00:09:59.899
the air circulation inside.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:00.933
Even though you're still hot,

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.034
it's impossible to be completely

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.569
cool inside.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:04.070
The whole thing

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.271
is like a giant chimney.

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:06.372
The bottom is a skirt

00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:07.440
, and the top opening

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:08.174
is from your side

00:10:08.174 --> 00:10:09.609
upwards,

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:10.042
so the heat

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:11.210
keeps circulating inside.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.178
That's why

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:13.179
many people in Arabia

00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:14.413
still like to wear that kind of clothing

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:15.748
—aside from traditional culture

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.316
and their formal attire.

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:18.517
Actually, I think it's

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:19.518
the coolest outfit

00:10:19.552 --> 00:10:20.953
I've ever worn in Arabia.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:21.887
So, the chimney effect

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:23.055
works on your body.

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:23.789
If your building

00:10:23.789 --> 00:10:24.924
could maintain airflow,

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:25.791
that would be great.

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:27.126
But

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:28.327
what you're afraid of when buildings need airflow is rain.

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:29.061
So, look at

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:29.829
this structure.

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:30.463
I wonder

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:31.764
how the rain gets in.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:32.732
Many people have racked their brains trying

00:10:32.732 --> 00:10:34.033
to find a way to ventilate

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:35.468
without leaking

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:36.535
, but

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:37.269
the solution

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:38.537
is like what you see in movies:

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:39.905
the internal structure of a skylight.

00:10:39.939 --> 00:10:41.474
This is called a staggered louver.

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:42.208
Simply put, it's

00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:43.476
a design with layers of

00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:44.777
crisscrossing guide plates

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:46.178
inside the ventilation duct.

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:47.179
Because air is gas... Gases

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:48.714
can bend and travel around,

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.116
so hot air can still

00:10:50.116 --> 00:10:51.384
escape through the gaps.

00:10:51.384 --> 00:10:53.119
However, rainwater is a liquid;

00:10:53.119 --> 00:10:53.986
it cannot bend

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:54.854
and must comply with

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:55.821
the principle of gravity.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:56.856
Therefore, raindrops

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:58.491
that hit the guide plate are blocked

00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:00.092
and flow down along it.

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:01.761
This staggered louver structure design

00:11:01.761 --> 00:11:02.495
prevents

00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:03.829
leaks during typhoons.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:05.131
This is

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:06.832
the core design that earned it a US patent.

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:07.400
Don't copy it, or

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.401
you'll be sued!

00:11:08.401 --> 00:11:09.769
And why can it let in light?

00:11:09.802 --> 00:11:10.970
Because its skylight top

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.004
uses translucent glass

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.339
to let in natural light

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:14.073
while keeping most of the heat

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:15.675
outside.

00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:16.575
Therefore, it can simultaneously

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:17.543
achieve… There are four key aspects

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:18.344
to consider :

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:19.178
lighting, ventilation

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:20.012
, heat dissipation, and

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:20.946
leak prevention.

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:21.881
When light enters,

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:22.915
it creates

00:11:22.915 --> 00:11:24.116
a unique heat effect

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:24.817
.

00:11:24.817 --> 00:11:25.985
This heat,

00:11:25.985 --> 00:11:27.119
by heating

00:11:27.153 --> 00:11:27.920
the device,

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.321
accelerates the chimney effect,

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:30.523
allowing heat to escape faster.

00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:31.023
Since

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:32.124
it was invented by Taiwanese people,

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:33.492
they are naturally familiar with

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:35.127
the various unusual architectural styles in Taiwan. Therefore, even

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:36.595
with the same modular principle

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:38.197
, there are four different types.

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:39.799
For example, there's the

00:11:39.799 --> 00:11:40.766
pull-to-open type

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:41.434
, and the

00:11:41.434 --> 00:11:43.069
hand-push type,

00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:44.770
which relates to whether or not people

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:45.538
need to go outside,

00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:46.272
because some workers... In factories

00:11:46.272 --> 00:11:47.239
, some

00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:47.873
people need to go outside.

00:11:47.873 --> 00:11:49.208
Some are housed in stacked shipping containers.

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:50.142
You need to go outside to

00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:51.243
plant flowers and grass,

00:11:51.243 --> 00:11:51.944
etc.

00:11:51.944 --> 00:11:53.079
I often see old men

00:11:53.079 --> 00:11:54.046
climbing outside their tin shacks,

00:11:54.046 --> 00:11:55.081
and I don't know what they're doing.

00:11:55.081 --> 00:11:56.315
Then there are

00:11:56.315 --> 00:11:57.016
electrically controlled systems.

00:11:57.016 --> 00:11:57.650
For example,

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:58.417
if you

00:11:58.417 --> 00:11:59.285
have this kind of equipment,

00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:00.519
and a fire breaks out, you

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:01.253
can use the electrical control

00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:02.054
to open it

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:02.955
and simultaneously ventilate the smoke

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:04.223
, giving people

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:05.157
more time to escape.

00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:05.825
And of course,

00:12:05.825 --> 00:12:06.726
when we first

00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:07.860
entered the factory,

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:08.394
you might notice that

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:09.829
even without turning on the lights

00:12:09.829 --> 00:12:10.796
, it's still brightly lit.

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:11.831
That's because it uses fixed lighting.

00:12:11.831 --> 00:12:13.165
Even without people going up

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:14.166
, you can still see that

00:12:14.166 --> 00:12:15.534
if you want the factory to be brighter,

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:16.469
you can install more lights

00:12:16.469 --> 00:12:18.270
, like openings in a factory.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.071
The more you open,

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:20.072
the brighter it is.

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:21.741
Although you might think it costs money

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:23.242
, if you think about it carefully,

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:24.176
the reason we

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:25.244
want to use this episode

00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:26.078
to introduce

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:27.246
this principle is important.

00:12:27.246 --> 00:12:27.913
It's a

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:29.081
system that doesn't use electricity,

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:30.750
doesn't require frequent maintenance

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.517
, and at the same time

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:33.085
helps with lighting,

00:12:33.085 --> 00:12:34.186
making your work

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:35.020
clearer

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.422
and improving ventilation.

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:37.156
Your factory

00:12:37.156 --> 00:12:38.524
, your small business owners,

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:39.592
your employees, and your colleagues

00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:40.326
can all

00:12:40.326 --> 00:12:41.260
work more comfortably.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.128
That's why

00:12:42.128 --> 00:12:43.262
this design has

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:44.163
won many awards

00:12:44.163 --> 00:12:44.964
abroad.

00:12:44.964 --> 00:12:45.598
It's because

00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:46.732
in Europe and America,

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:47.967
ventilation

00:12:47.967 --> 00:12:49.135
is highly valued.

00:12:49.135 --> 00:12:50.035
In Europe,

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:51.270
heating is frequently

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:51.937
used to

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:53.506
maintain temperature

00:12:53.506 --> 00:12:55.174
, but ventilation is also essential.

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:55.841
Germans, in particular

00:12:55.841 --> 00:12:56.675
, insist on

00:12:56.675 --> 00:12:58.077
ventilating every room every morning

00:12:58.077 --> 00:12:58.611
to ensure

00:12:58.611 --> 00:12:59.912
the air is clean.

00:12:59.912 --> 00:13:00.613
A Taiwanese-German told me

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:02.114
this, and her husband said the same

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:03.382
. Some Germans

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:04.250
don't have this habit,

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.017
but

00:13:05.017 --> 00:13:06.485
the comments below

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:07.353
highlight how much

00:13:07.353 --> 00:13:07.953
they value ventilation

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:09.421
. Especially now, Europe

00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:10.289
is getting hotter and hotter.

00:13:10.289 --> 00:13:11.323
You know, electric fans have appeared

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:12.591
in Europe in recent years

00:13:12.591 --> 00:13:14.460
– what an amazing discovery!

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.861
Before, there were

00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:16.962
no electric fans in Europe,

00:13:16.962 --> 00:13:17.763
no need for air conditioning.

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:18.731
But now,

00:13:18.731 --> 00:13:19.465
if you travel to Europe,

00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:20.566
you might encounter

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:21.734
very stuffy rooms

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:23.035
. If you see a

00:13:23.035 --> 00:13:24.103
hotel without air conditioning,

00:13:24.103 --> 00:13:25.037
I suggest Taiwanese people

00:13:25.037 --> 00:13:25.971
don't stay there;

00:13:25.971 --> 00:13:27.139
you won't be able to stand it.

00:13:27.139 --> 00:13:28.007
Therefore, these kinds of devices

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:28.908
are becoming increasingly common.

00:13:28.908 --> 00:13:29.708
But so far, we've

00:13:29.708 --> 00:13:30.843
only seen them on display.

00:13:30.843 --> 00:13:31.544
Let me take you

00:13:31.544 --> 00:13:33.345
to the sales office to see

00:13:33.345 --> 00:13:35.014
what it looks like .

00:13:35.014 --> 00:13:36.115
It looks like a

00:13:36.115 --> 00:13:37.416
small metal box

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:38.751
, but from below, it looks

00:13:38.751 --> 00:13:40.452
like this.

00:13:42.588 --> 00:13:43.689
But I want to tell you,

00:13:43.689 --> 00:13:44.757
do you see this ladder

00:13:45.524 --> 00:13:46.525
? Isn't it different

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:48.093
? It still goes to the rooftop

00:13:48.093 --> 00:13:49.261
, but the experience

00:13:49.261 --> 00:13:49.962
is completely different

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:51.797
. And it folds up

00:13:52.364 --> 00:13:53.232
very small!

00:13:58.237 --> 00:13:59.071
Imagine this:

00:13:59.071 --> 00:14:00.072
in this place

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:01.941
, there are bookshelves all over the back. If

00:14:01.941 --> 00:14:03.275
you want to move to the second floor,

00:14:03.275 --> 00:14:05.344
you can use it as a display shelf.

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:06.612
Or, in some

00:14:06.612 --> 00:14:08.447
homes, it

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:10.049
's partitioned into a mezzanine,

00:14:10.049 --> 00:14:11.517
and you can extend it to

00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:12.718
become a ladder.

00:14:12.718 --> 00:14:14.420
If you want to fold it up today,

00:14:15.721 --> 00:14:16.856
you can fold it up

00:14:18.224 --> 00:14:19.992
and clip it on the side.

00:14:19.992 --> 00:14:20.860
So, you see, this

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.194
skylight for lighting and ventilation,

00:14:22.194 --> 00:14:23.329
when it's installed today,

00:14:23.329 --> 00:14:24.597
the supporting components below

00:14:24.597 --> 00:14:25.464
are also done for you.

00:14:25.464 --> 00:14:26.999
And if you close it, if

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:30.636
I don't want to go out today,

00:14:30.636 --> 00:14:31.403
or if it rains,

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:32.838
I can close it up.

00:14:32.838 --> 00:14:35.507
You see,

00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:36.775
this is what you see now.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:37.643
But do you remember

00:14:37.643 --> 00:14:38.777
what your traditional things

00:14:38.777 --> 00:14:39.612
looked like

00:14:39.612 --> 00:14:40.880
? The old ones looked like

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:41.981
this. Isn't this familiar

00:14:41.981 --> 00:14:43.382
? When you were a child

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:45.551
, didn't you climb these kinds of round poles

00:14:45.551 --> 00:14:46.518
before they were fixed?

00:14:46.518 --> 00:14:47.686
But when they were actually fixed,

00:14:47.686 --> 00:14:48.654
they looked like this

00:14:48.654 --> 00:14:50.556
, completely at a 90-degree angle

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:52.091
. In our kind of detached houses,

00:14:52.091 --> 00:14:53.759
there are usually water towers installed on top.

00:14:53.759 --> 00:14:55.294
When you need to go up to repair something,

00:14:55.294 --> 00:14:55.861
you have to go up.

00:14:55.861 --> 00:14:56.395
So, at this time,

00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:57.630
you have to carry your tool bag

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.064
and grab this

00:14:59.064 --> 00:15:00.900
to climb up.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:01.667
But this

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:02.735
is not the most difficult part

00:15:02.735 --> 00:15:04.436
. What is the most difficult part?

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:06.605
You have to push open the cover on top first.

00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:07.740
In the past,

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.141
some construction companies would install this,

00:15:09.141 --> 00:15:09.975
which made it very difficult to climb

00:15:09.975 --> 00:15:11.911
. Otherwise... They'll leave you an A-frame ladder

00:15:11.911 --> 00:15:12.678
like this.

00:15:12.678 --> 00:15:14.647
You can put your tools on the ground first,

00:15:14.647 --> 00:15:15.848
then

00:15:15.848 --> 00:15:16.782
climb

00:15:16.782 --> 00:15:17.683
up ,

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:18.851
climb up ,

00:15:18.851 --> 00:15:19.952
climb up, climb up, climb up, climb up.

00:15:19.952 --> 00:15:20.719
Then

00:15:20.719 --> 00:15:21.520
you can see

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:22.655
what kind of lighting

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:24.056
this building should have.

00:15:24.056 --> 00:15:25.257
I need to pry it open

00:15:25.257 --> 00:15:27.126
(it's strenuous).

00:15:27.126 --> 00:15:28.727
Usually, we'll use our

00:15:28.727 --> 00:15:30.262
heads to support it

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:32.298
, then lift your body up first,

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:35.567
and then lift it open.

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:37.569
This is the traditional way of opening it.

00:15:37.569 --> 00:15:39.371
So, this is the kind

00:15:39.371 --> 00:15:41.774
of lighting and natural light the roof should have.

00:15:41.774 --> 00:15:42.775
But have you noticed

00:15:42.775 --> 00:15:43.575
my hands

00:15:43.575 --> 00:15:44.777
aren't afraid of getting hot?

00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:45.644
After all , I

00:15:45.644 --> 00:15:47.346
used to be a blacksmith.

00:15:47.346 --> 00:15:48.881
But normally, with this kind of traditional

00:15:48.881 --> 00:15:49.648
tin roof,

00:15:49.648 --> 00:15:50.382
firstly,

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:51.250
you see, it's very difficult to open.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.584
Actually, you see, it's a thin piece.

00:15:52.584 --> 00:15:54.286
Just now, I had to lift it up,

00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:55.487
which was quite strenuous.

00:15:55.487 --> 00:15:56.622
I had to use my biceps.

00:15:56.622 --> 00:15:58.490
Also, it might get sunburned.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:15:59.391
If it's midday and

00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:00.426
the water tower breaks,

00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:01.527
it will be very painful to repair.

00:16:01.527 --> 00:16:02.528
Thirdly, there's no ventilation

00:16:02.528 --> 00:16:03.562
and no natural light.

00:16:03.562 --> 00:16:05.230
Next, what's even more inconvenient is the ladder.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.299
You either have to choose one that's hard to climb

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:08.767
or an A-frame ladder,

00:16:08.767 --> 00:16:09.435
which is easier to climb

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:10.769
but very inconvenient

00:16:10.769 --> 00:16:11.470
and

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.138
takes up a lot of space in your house.

00:16:13.539 --> 00:16:15.074
Did I just not take the tools up?

00:16:15.074 --> 00:16:16.342
Then there's the A-frame ladder.

00:16:19.478 --> 00:16:20.412
So, at this point, you have to go down

00:16:20.412 --> 00:16:21.413
, then put the tools up again,

00:16:21.413 --> 00:16:22.748
and then start your repairs.

00:16:22.748 --> 00:16:24.616
This is the troublesome part of the traditional method

00:16:24.616 --> 00:16:25.651
. Metal covers

00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:27.186
not only help heat your house

00:16:27.186 --> 00:16:29.521
but also create many maintenance difficulties

00:16:29.521 --> 00:16:31.056
and block natural light.

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:32.391
So, you see the difference?

00:16:32.391 --> 00:16:33.325
From elementary school engineering

00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:34.226
to growing up and making big money,

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:35.461
it can also help

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:36.161
improve ventilation

00:16:36.161 --> 00:16:37.629
and make your living environment better.

00:16:37.629 --> 00:16:39.098
So, whether you own a factory, a

00:16:39.098 --> 00:16:39.698
metal

00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:41.967
shed , a detached house

00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:43.902
, or are currently building a high-rise ,

00:16:43.902 --> 00:16:44.803
are an interior designer

00:16:44.803 --> 00:16:45.371
or a developer

00:16:45.371 --> 00:16:46.638
, and don't want to spend a lot of money

00:16:46.638 --> 00:16:47.272
on air conditioning

00:16:47.272 --> 00:16:48.974
to cool your house later, if you want

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:50.342
to lower your house temperature

00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:51.443
using a completely

00:16:51.443 --> 00:16:53.012
natural and scientific method

00:16:53.012 --> 00:16:54.747
, utilizing the chimney effect,

00:16:54.747 --> 00:16:56.015
then you can consider

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.316
this new approach.

00:16:57.316 --> 00:16:58.083
You can search online for

00:16:58.083 --> 00:16:59.518
information on skylights for lighting and ventilation.

00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:00.619
This isn't just a young team

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:02.087
; it's a Taiwanese patent.

